 {:id "adr-2607062330-kototama-tender-chicory-execution-runtime"
  :title "ADR-2607062330: kototama.tender — the Chicory/JVM execution runtime ADR-2607022900 decided on, landed"
  :status "accepted"
  :date "2026-07-06"
  :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"]
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "kototama-tender-chicory-execution-runtime"
  :authoritative true
  :authoritative_for
  ["kototama.tender (kototama/src/kototama/tender.clj, :clj-only) is the first real execution layer for kototama.contract's HostCaps/RuntimeLimits/validate-import-surface -- pure data validation now has something that actually enforces it"
   "written fresh, not vendored from kotoba.wasm-exec, to avoid running kotoba's own incompatible kgraph/capability vocabulary alongside kototama's actor:host ABI (ADR-2607022700's semantic-authority-duplication rule)"
   "two distinct denial shapes: grant violation (:grant/missing) hard-throws (structural authority breach, not guest-recoverable); RuntimeLimits exhaustion signals in-band as -1 (same convention as write-bytes!'s overflow case, a guest can see it and back off) -- do not conflate the two"
   "ADR-2607022900's claim that quota/fuel/etc landed in aiueos-cljc-contract PRs #2-12 is verified FALSE (no such files/deps/commits exist in that repo) -- this ADR is the first with actually-running tender code"
   "verified against real Wasm binaries: wasm-tools-assembled WAT fixtures through the real Chicory Parser/Instance pipeline, not mocked -- 15 tests/31 assertions green"
   "addendum: aiueos.execute/aiueos.launcher (aiueos-cljc-contract's real main) already implements a similar-looking Chicory-hosted capability-gated execution path under aiueos's own manifest/broker vocabulary -- DECIDED to keep the two separate (different vocabularies for different problems: kototama.contract's cross-substrate actor:host ABI vs aiueos's OS-broker manifest/quota/topic/device vocabulary), not consolidate; aiueos calling kototama.tender/instantiate (translating a broker decision into a HostCaps value) remains an open follow-up, distinct from a code-level merge"
   "addendum 2: :max-memory-pages added to kototama.contract/RuntimeLimits (default 16 pages/1 MiB) and enforced in kototama.tender via Chicory's STABLE Instance.Builder/withMemoryLimits (not the :unsafe fuel-listener API tier), independent of which imports are granted -- 18 tests/35 assertions green"
   "addendum 3: verified kotoba wasm emit CANNOT call these 8 actor:host imports from real .kotoba source today -- the compiler resolves host-import calls against a CLOSED, hardcoded table (kotoba-core-contracts/resources/kotoba/runtime/capability_contract.edn's :host-imports/:host-import-order, merged with kotoba.runtime/cap-passing-imports), with no source-level FFI/import-declaration syntax; extending that table (in kotoba-core-contracts and kotoba, not kototama) is a prerequisite for a real .kotoba-source end-to-end test, tracked as a follow-up, not yet done"
   "addendum 4: :now/:log-append! renamed to :clock-monotonic/:log-write (kototama#21) to reuse names a concurrent session had already independently registered in kotoba-core-contracts' capability_contract.edn for aiueos's kernel-capability vocabulary (identical wire signatures) -- full detail and the matching wasm-webcomponent/kototama-web renames in ADR-2607062400's addendum"]
